    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] controls the location of the developer directory used by [[p1]], [[p2]], [[p3]], and other Xcode and BSD development tools. This also controls the locations that are searched for by [[p4]] for developer tool manpages.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "xcode-select"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "xcrun(1)"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "xcodebuild(1)"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "cc(1)"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "man(1)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This allows you to easily switch between different versions of the Xcode tools and can be used to update the path to the Xcode if it is moved after installation.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Usage",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "When multiple Xcode applications are installed on a system (e.g. [[p0]], containing the latest Xcode, and [[p1]] containing a beta) use [[p2]] [[p3]][[p4]] path/to/Xcode.app[[p5]] to specify the Xcode that you wish to use for command line developer tools.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "/Applications/Xcode.app"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "/Applications/Xcode-beta.app"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "xcode-select"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "--switch"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "After setting a developer directory, all of the [[p0]] provided developer tool shims (see [[p1]]) will automatically invoke the version of the tool inside the selected developer directory. Your own scripts, makefiles, and other tools can also use [[p2]] to easily lookup tools inside the active developer directory, making it easy to switch them between different versions of the Xcode tools and allowing them to function properly on systems where the Xcode application has been installed to a non-default location.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "xcode-select"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "FILES"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "xcrun(1)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
